{"type":"message","id":"0efeedb3","parentId":"71e802c5","timestamp":"2026-03-14T16:23:55.660Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"217976313","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# LESSONS.md - Recursive Learning\n\nThis file is your system memory for errors, anti-patterns, and successful strategies. **Read this file at the start of every session.**\n\n## 🚫 Avoid These Mistakes (Anti-Patterns)\n- **LM Studio Auth**: LM Studio / Local models often require a dummy `apiKey` (e.g., \"lm-studio\") even if they don't use it. Errors about \"No API key found\" usually mean this is missing in `openclaw.json`.\n- **PowerShell Execution**: In Windows, `openclaw.ps1` may be blocked by execution policies. Always use `Set-ExecutionPolicy RemoteSigned -Scope CurrentUser` to fix this first.\n- **Port Conflicts**: If the gateway restart fails, a stale `node.exe` is likely on port 18789. Use `Stop-Process -Id <PID>` or `netstat` to find and kill it.\n- **ClawHub Multi-Install**: `clawhub install` only takes one slug at a time. Do not pass multiple slugs in one command.\n\n## ✅ Golden Rules\n- **Windows Command Mastery**: Always check if a command exists with `where` or `Get-Command` before relying on it.\n- **Git State**: All projects in `D:\\AI_PROJECTS\\projects` are standalone. Always `cd` into the specific project folder before running `git` commands.\n- **Skill Usage**:\n    - `summarize`: Use it before reading files > 100 lines.\n    - `ui-ux-pro-max-plus`: Use it for ALL CSS/Styling tasks.\n    - `gitflow`: Use it for all feature work in `D:\\AI_PROJECTS`.\n\n## 📈 Learning History\n- **2026-03-14**: Initial system setup. Resolved LM Studio auth issue. Configured Tailscale Serve. Installed 5 core skills. Reworked UI-UX skill to English.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1773505435659}}
